= Practice Questions — Part 1 (Q1 to Q5)

#mcq(1, [Amniocentesis is a clinical procedure legally permitted in India solely for which of the following medical indications?], (
  [Prenatal sex determination to maintain family gender balance],
  [Detecting foetal chromosomal aneuploidies such as Down syndrome and metabolic disorders],
  [Assessing maternal pelvic dimensions prior to vaginal delivery],
  [Inducing selective abortion of female foetuses in high-parity mothers],
))
#solution(1, [Amniocentesis is a prenatal diagnostic technique wherein amniotic fluid containing foetal skin and mucosal cells is aspirated to detect chromosomal abnormalities (e.g., Down syndrome, Turner syndrome, Klinefelter syndrome) and inborn metabolic disorders (e.g., PKU). Under the PCPNDT Act 1994, its use for prenatal sex determination is strictly banned to eradicate female foeticide.], answer: [B])

#mcq(2, [Which of the following represents an essential pharmacological attribute of an ideal contraceptive device?], (
  [It must irreversibly block gametogenesis in both partners],
  [It must be user-friendly, highly effective, completely reversible, with minimal side effects],
  [It must permanently eliminate secondary sexual characteristics to suppress libido],
  [It must act strictly post-implantation by inducing chemical abortion],
))
#solution(2, [According to NCERT, an ideal contraceptive must be user-friendly, easily available, effective, completely reversible with no or least side effects, and must not interfere with the user's normal sexual drive, desire, or the sexual act. Contraceptives prevent conception, rather than inducing abortion post-implantation.], answer: [B])

#mcq(3, [Lactational amenorrhea functions as an effective natural birth control method primarily because:], (
  [Placental progesterone persists in maternal circulation for up to 12 months],
  [Intense infant suckling elevates prolactin, suppressing pulsatile GnRH and gonadotropin secretion],
  [Maternal glycogen reserves are exhausted, inhibiting ovarian follicular angiogenesis],
  [Oxytocin release causes continuous uterine contractions that dislodge unfertilized ova],
))
#solution(3, [Post-partum intense suckling by the infant stimulates maternal prolactin secretion. Elevated prolactin exerts negative feedback on the hypothalamus, suppressing pulsatile GnRH release. Consequently, anterior pituitary FSH and LH surges are abolished, preventing follicular growth and ovulation. This natural method is effective for a maximum duration of 6 months post-partum.], answer: [B])

#mcq(4, [What is the precise cellular mechanism of action by which copper-releasing IUDs (such as CuT, Cu7, and Multiload 375) prevent pregnancy?], (
  [They induce permanent surgical occlusion of the bilateral fallopian tubes],
  [Released copper ions suppress sperm motility and fertilizing capacity while stimulating phagocytosis of sperms],
  [They prevent ovulation by maintaining high circulating levels of progesterone],
  [They dissolve the zona pellucida of the secondary oocyte inside the ovary],
))
#solution(4, [Copper-releasing IUDs (CuT, Cu7, Multiload 375) continuously elute ionized copper ($"Cu"^(2+)$) into the uterine lumen. Copper ions suppress sperm motility, impair sperm flagellar kinematics, and destroy sperm fertilizing capacity, while the physical presence of the IUD promotes macrophage phagocytosis of spermatozoa in the uterine cavity.], answer: [B])

#mcq(5, [How do hormone-releasing intrauterine devices such as Progestasert and LNG-20 primarily execute their contraceptive function?], (
  [By releasing cytotoxic heavy metals that destroy endometrial stroma],
  [By rendering the endometrium unsuitable for implantation and making the cervix hostile to sperms],
  [By chemically hydrolyzing the acrosome of mature spermatozoa inside the vagina],
  [By stimulating pituitary LH surge to accelerate premature luteinization],
))
#solution(5, [Hormone-releasing IUDs (Progestasert, LNG-20) slowly release progestin locally within the uterus. This induces endometrial glandular atrophy, rendering the endometrium completely unreceptive to blastocyst implantation, and thickens cervical mucus into a tenacious barrier hostile to sperm penetration.], answer: [B])

#pagebreak()

= Practice Questions — Part 2 (Q6 to Q10)

#mcq(6, [The oral contraceptive pill 'Saheli', developed by scientists at CDRI Lucknow, is unique because it is:], (
  [A steroidal pill containing high-dose testosterone taken daily for 21 days],
  [A non-steroidal formulation (Centchroman) taken once a week with minimal side effects],
  [An emergency pill that must be administered within 24 hours of coitus],
  [An injectable depot progestogen administered subcutaneously once every 5 years],
))
#solution(6, [Saheli (Centchroman / Ormeloxifene) is the world's first non-steroidal oral contraceptive pill, engineered by the Central Drug Research Institute (CDRI) in Lucknow, India. It acts as a selective estrogen receptor modulator that prevents blastocyst implantation. It is taken twice weekly for the first 3 months and once weekly thereafter, exhibiting negligible side effects.], answer: [B])

#mcq(7, [To prevent potential conception following unprotected intercourse, sexual assault, or contraceptive failure, emergency contraceptives must be administered within a strict window of:], (
  [24 hours of coitus],
  [72 hours of coitus],
  [7 days of coitus],
  [14 days of coitus],
))
#solution(7, [Emergency contraceptives (such as progestogens alone, progestogen-estrogen combination pills, or insertion of an IUD) are clinically proven to be highly effective if administered within a strict threshold of *72 hours (3 days)* following unprotected intercourse, rape, or barrier malfunction.], answer: [B])

#mcq(8, [Following a successful bilateral vasectomy in a human male, which of the following physiological statements is completely ACCURATE?], (
  [The patient immediately ceases to synthesize testosterone and loses secondary sex traits],
  [The volume of ejaculate is drastically reduced to zero],
  [Spermatogenesis continues in the testes, but the ejaculated semen lacks spermatozoa],
  [Spermatozoa are diverted into the ureters and excreted during micturition],
))
#solution(8, [Vasectomy involves cutting and ligating a small section of both vasa deferentia. Because Leydig cells remain completely intact, testicular testosterone secretion and male secondary sexual traits remain normal. Spermatogenesis continues in the seminiferous tubules, but the sperms cannot traverse the severed duct and are phagocytosed. Ejaculate volume remains almost normal, but contains zero sperms (azoospermia).], answer: [C])

#mcq(9, [Under the Medical Termination of Pregnancy (MTP) Amendment Act 2017 of India, up to how many weeks of gestation is an abortion considered safest and requires the opinion of only one Registered Medical Practitioner?], (
  [Up to 6 weeks],
  [Up to 12 weeks (First Trimester)],
  [Up to 20 weeks],
  [Up to 28 weeks],
))
#solution(9, [Under the MTP Act, abortion is legally permitted and medically safest during the *first trimester (up to 12 weeks of pregnancy)*, requiring the diagnostic opinion of *one Registered Medical Practitioner*. Second-trimester terminations (12 to 20 weeks) carry significantly higher maternal morbidity and mandate the concurring opinion of *two Registered Medical Practitioners*.], answer: [B])

#mcq(10, [Which of the following groups contains EXCLUSIVELY sexually transmitted infections that are currently completely INCURABLE?], (
  [Gonorrhoea, Syphilis, and Trichomoniasis],
  [Hepatitis B, Genital Herpes, and HIV/AIDS],
  [Chlamydiasis, Genital Warts, and Syphilis],
  [Trichomoniasis, Hepatitis B, and Gonorrhoea],
))
#solution(10, [According to NCERT Class 12 Biology, except for *Hepatitis B*, *Genital Herpes*, and *HIV infection*, all other sexually transmitted infections (such as Gonorrhoea, Syphilis, Chlamydiasis, and Trichomoniasis) are completely curable if diagnosed early and treated properly with appropriate antibiotics or antiparasitics.], answer: [B])

